    "title": "Surgeon with 25 years of experience warns less than 6 hours of sleep can increase risk of heart disease, certain cancers | Health",
    "text": "The U-shaped curve of health risk\nDr London shared that when it comes to rest, more isn't always better, and less is definitely dangerous. He described the relationship between sleep duration and health risks as a U-shaped curve. According to him, sleeping fewer than 6 hours or more than 9 hours was dangerous, while the sweet spot was aiming for 6 to 8 hours of quality rest.",
